Negative control for pager-writes-through-criteria.int.test.ts.

Pins the pager write-through law in useQuery.ts: `pageIndex`'s setter writes
the cursor THROUGH the criteria's own `pagination.offset`. The mutation pins
the outbound offset to 0, so every "next page" repeats page 1 while the pager
claims to have moved.

The law is useQuery.ts's, but a bare `useQuery().list()` never issues its
first fetch in this harness, so the walk is driven end to end through the
migrated client-address module — which is why this mutant lives beside that
spec rather than under modules/query.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

